course: dictionary
lesson: 1787
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word clip has several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. A clip can be a small object that holds things together, or a short piece of a video. «Morven borrows Iona's glittery hair clips for a party» tells you a clip is something that holds hair in place.
explain: Clip can also be a doing word. To clip can mean to fasten something with a clip, or to cut small bits off with scissors. Ask yourself what is being done. In «clip the badge onto your coat» you fasten. In «clip the hedge» you cut.
explain: «One clip shows one moment, not the whole person.» Here clip means a short piece of a film or video. The words around it, one moment and the whole person, are your clues.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right. If it does not, try another meaning from the list.
fact: A clip is a small object that holds things together or in place, like a paper clip or a hair clip.
fact: To clip means to fasten with a clip, as in «clip the badge onto your coat».
fact: To clip also means to cut small bits off, as in «clip your nails» or «clip the hedge».
fact: A clip is a short piece of a film or video, such as a six-second video clip.
fact: To clip can mean to hit lightly at the edge, as in «the car clipped the kerb».
exercise: Morven says, «Ah, they're braw, cheers, wee yin» about Iona's hair clips. What is a hair clip? | *A small fastener that holds hair in place | A brush for combing hair | A short video of a party | A pair of scissors for cutting hair
exercise: What does clip mean in «clip the hedge»? | To fasten with a clip | A short piece of a film | *To cut small bits off with scissors or clippers | To hit lightly at the edge
exercise: «One clip shows one moment, not the whole person.» What does clip mean here? | To hit lightly | *A short piece of a film or video | A small metal fastener | To cut small bits off
test: «The car clipped the kerb.» What does clipped mean here? | Watched on a tablet | Cut with scissors | *Hit lightly at the edge | Held together with a clip
test: «Hold a paper clip under a table and move a magnet on top.» What is a paper clip? | A short video | *A small metal object that holds papers together | A type of pen | A tool for cutting paper
exam: Which sentence uses clip to mean a short piece of a video? | «The clip is in the drawer.» | «Clip the badge onto your coat.» | *«A six-second clip can hide what came before and after.» | «Clip the hedge this weekend, please.»
